From 76236e116bcce7ff6b16cabde3eca2c84024c39f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:48:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(delegation): ended-parent sweep resolves the
 delegator past compression; spares pinned rows; recovery ends a compressed
 child's open tip

Follow-up to review 5878780845 of #1600 (non-blocking points S1-S3).

- S1: end_subagents_of_ended_parents judged a subagent row by its immediate
  parent. A compressed child's continuation has its own compressed segment as
  parent (end_reason='compression', always ended), so it was reaped while the
  delegating parent was still open. The sweep now walks up the row's own
  subagent compression segments (_delegating_parent_on) and requires that
  delegator to be ended.
- S2: exclude_pinned, as in sweep_orphaned_sessions (pinned rows and the
  unpinned continuations a pinned segment covers); the startup reaper passes
  exclude_pinned=True like its orphan sweep.
- S3: recovery / stall force-finalize ended only the ids persisted at dispatch;
  after a child compressed, its open row is a continuation of that id. They now
  end the open rows of each verified child's compression lineage (a delegate
  child of a segment is not a continuation and stays open).
- end_terminal_unit_children docstring: a worker process's units are not
  covered by owner recovery; say what actually closes them.
